From a84f8012eeda28fb15b0e767acb93d72d2520fac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 04:00:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Float bounds: warnings for double only, tests with
 mfront-query

- The bounded default perturbation of the numerical jacobian (a tenth of
  the convergence criterion) is raised without warning: every implicit
  behaviour without @PerturbationValueForNumericalJacobianComputation
  reported it with float.
- The advice of the warnings on the convergence criteria (values too
  stringent or too loose, default value, 1e-14 being a good choice) is
  written for double: with float, these warnings are not reported, the
  value given by @Epsilon being bounded with its own warning, and the
  default value (1e-8) being close to the bound.
- mfront-query tests: the convergence criterion and the perturbation of
  AgeingBurger (@Epsilon 1e-11, default perturbation) are unchanged with
  double and raised to 1.19209e-08 and 1.19209e-07 with float; the default
  criterion of Norton (isotropic DSL) stays 1e-08 with float. The arguments
  of these tests may be a list.
- release notes: default criterion kept, default perturbation raised
  without warning, criterion of @CompareToNumericalJacobian to give with
  float.
---
 docs/web/release-notes-5.2.md                 |  9 ++++++-
 mfront-query/tests/CMakeLists.txt             | 22 +++++++++++++++-
 ...geingburger-convergence-criteria-float.ref |  2 ++
 ...uery-ageingburger-convergence-criteria.ref |  2 ++
 ...ery-norton-convergence-criterion-float.ref |  1 +
